People often compare $CCD to Worldcoin or ICP.

I think that comparison misses the bigger picture.

@worldnetwork focuses on proving personhood.

@dfinity provides the infrastructure layer for AI applications.

@Concordium is tackling a different challenge: creating a trust layer for AI agents.

Through zero knowledge proofs (ZKPs), support across ETH, SOL, and CCD, and verifiable identities, agents can prove that a real accountable person or organization stands behind them without exposing their actual identity.

As AI agents become more widespread, trust, accountability, and verification will be essential.

That's one of the key reasons I'm very bullish on $CCD.
